WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.760
If I asked you what the largest e-commerce
company in the world was...

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.750
I bet most of you would answer Amazon without even hesitating.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:06.750
However, folks…

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:13.070
That may not be the case.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:24.630
Listen up.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:41.450
With

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:46.520
a market value of more than 400 billion dollars
and more than 600 million customers worldwide,

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:51.640
Alibaba, an incredible success story, is also
the most valuable Chinese company in the world.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:56.190
We could say that this company has become
the best representative of the new Chinese

00:00:56.190 --> 00:01:03.550
capitalism.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:07.130
Let's go back for a second to the question
that we asked at the beginning of this video.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:10.899
Is Amazon the largest e-commerce company in
the world?

00:01:10.899 --> 00:01:14.560
Well... it depends.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:21.599
If, for example, we take a look at the market
value, that is, how much investors value the

00:01:21.599 --> 00:01:24.829
company... then undoubtedly, Amazon is the
largest company.

00:01:24.829 --> 00:01:29.179
But if instead we focus on the volume of sales
made through the company every year, that

00:01:29.179 --> 00:01:34.670
is, where more goods are bought and sold…
then Alibaba wins by a landslide.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:41.640
Yes, Alibaba may not be as popular and as
well-known as Amazon… after all, it mostly

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:46.409
works in the Asian market... but although
it may seem far away, products worth a total

00:01:46.409 --> 00:01:54.110
of more than 750 billion dollars are sold
each year through Alibaba’s different platforms.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:02:00.969
Now... those of you who usually follow VisualPolitik,
surely won’t be surprised by what I’m

00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:01.969
saying.

00:02:01.969 --> 00:02:07.420
Asia is undergoing a revolution... a takeoff,
an unprecedented economic growth process.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:12.090
Every year, around 160 million people leave
poverty behind and manage to become part of

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.180
the middle class...

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.290
160 million people in Asia alone.

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:20.120
In just a few years, countries like the Philippines
and Thailand will have middle classes as large

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.950
as those in the United Kingdom, France or
Italy.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:23.950
And then there's China...

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:29.090
whose middle class is... exploding, taking
off almost vertically.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:34.900
So, what happens when a person leaves poverty
behind and becomes part of the middle class?

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:38.190
Well... among other things, it means they
now have much more money to spend.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:43.530
That explains why the Chinese retail market
has multiplied by 4 in the last 5 years and

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:47.630
why forecasts indicate that the growth of
Chinese consumption in the next 3 to 4 years

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:54.170
will be greater than everything that the British
or Germans consume today.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:03:00.680
And... do you know who holds more than 70%
of the market share in China's e-commerce

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:08.200
sector and is very well positioned in the
other fastest growing Asian countries?

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:15.189
Exactly, Alibaba.

00:03:15.189 --> 00:03:25.620
I’m sure by now you’re beginning to see
this company under a different light.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:34.070
But before we take a look at Alibaba’s characteristics,
its light and dark side... let's see where

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.980
and how it all began.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:41.140
Let's see, its history.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:45.930
(JACK MA’S MIRACLE)

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:51.300
He was never the best student, but thanks
to the foreign tourists who visited his hometown

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:55.790
and especially to the relationship he developed
with an Australian family, Jack Ma, a child

00:03:55.790 --> 00:04:00.360
born in a humble family just 2 years before
Mao’s cultural revolution, managed to learn

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:03.819
English and acquired all the advantages offered
by the modern world.

00:04:03.819 --> 00:04:08.989
And as is often the in life, it wasn’t his
formal studies but the small experiences--the

00:04:08.989 --> 00:04:14.769
kind we often don’t even pay attention to--that
fed the success of the person who is, today,

00:04:14.769 --> 00:04:16.730
the richest man in all of China.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.949
(“I’m 100% ‘made in China.’

00:04:19.949 --> 00:04:23.800
I learned English myself, and I know nothing
about technology.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:28.340
[...] One of the reasons why Alibaba survived
is because I know nothing about computers.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:32.580
I’m like a blind man riding on the back
of a blind tiger.”

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.580
Jack Ma.)

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:37.669
Jack Ma, one of the heroes of the new modern
China, didn’t have the opportunity to attend

00:04:37.669 --> 00:04:38.669
a good university.

00:04:38.669 --> 00:04:42.229
However, since he learned English, he managed
to graduate with a teaching degree, got a

00:04:42.229 --> 00:04:46.240
job as a language teacher and a few years
later launched a translation company.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:49.741
And it was on a trip to the United States
to perform a translation service... that some

00:04:49.741 --> 00:04:54.360
friends from Seattle showed him what was then
an incipient technology called the Internet.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.139
At that moment, an idea hit Jack right in
the face.

00:04:57.139 --> 00:05:01.550
(“I was afraid of touching the computer
because it seemed very expensive, but they

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.520
said: ‘Come on, Jack, go ahead.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:04.800
It's not a bomb!’

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:11.250
Then I typed the word beer: B-E-E-R, and I
could see German and Japanese beer, but not

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.490
Chinese beer.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:15.490
Then I typed the word China and the answer
was ‘No results’.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:19.919
Then I thought: How interesting, if we could
group all the companies in China and create

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:23.290
a page for them, maybe we would achieve something
big.)”

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:26.210
And that’s precisely what he did.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:27.750
After returning to China...

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:32.480
Jack set up a company, China Pages, to list,
classify and thus find Chinese companies...

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.130
something like the yellow pages.

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:38.900
This company didn’t have the expected success,
but Jack learned enough to be ready for his

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.040
next adventure.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.680
After a lot of work in his small apartment,
both he and a team he’d managed to train

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:49.180
without virtually any resources, created Alibaba
in 1999, and it is now one of the largest

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:53.849
companies on the planet.

00:05:53.849 --> 00:06:00.720
(THE GREAT MARKET)

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:06.080
More than wondering what Alibaba does, we
should ask ourselves what it doesn’t do.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.129
Because… see…

00:06:08.129 --> 00:06:12.949
Alibaba isn’t a simple e-commerce portal,
but rather a kind of technological intermediary.

00:06:12.949 --> 00:06:18.750
In other words, unlike Amazon, Alibaba doesn’t
sell anything directly, but basically functions

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:24.020
as a large market where thousands and thousands
of brands, producers and distribution companies

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.849
sell their products to millions of customers.

00:06:26.849 --> 00:06:31.020
That is, Alibaba is the owner company, the
company that manages this huge market... and

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:34.790
supplies everything that brands, producers
and distributors need to be able to carry

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:38.210
out their business... from payment platforms
to metadata.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:42.270
In fact, this may be its biggest difference
with Amazon.

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:46.620
For example, think about the huge amount of
data that these companies handle: consumer

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:49.920
trends, budgets, types of customers, purchase
timing, etcetera, etcetera.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:54.300
Well, while Amazon uses all that data to develop
its own product lines....

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.229
Alibaba shares them with the companies that
operate through their markets... so that they

00:06:57.229 --> 00:07:02.419
can launch new products or... know their consumers’
preferences better and thus sell more, making

00:07:02.419 --> 00:07:05.569
the market grow, which makes Alibaba grow.

00:07:05.569 --> 00:07:11.610
Thus, over time, Alibaba has developed several
different markets...

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:15.590
So if you’d like, to better understand what
Alibaba is exactly, let's take a look at what

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:19.270
these markets are and how they differ.

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:24.770
First of all, we have Alibaba.com a huge wholesale
market, perhaps the largest online wholesale

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:25.819
market on the planet.

00:07:25.819 --> 00:07:28.240
That is to say, this market isn’t aimed
at consumers.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:32.389
Through this space, producers, manufacturers
sell their products in bulk to other companies

00:07:32.389 --> 00:07:36.090
so they can distribute them in their countries.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:39.819
For example, say you have a store and want
to order 5,000 red shirts with a specific

00:07:39.819 --> 00:07:40.819
logo.

00:07:40.819 --> 00:07:42.180
This is the place for you.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:47.240
(“Unless we use Alibaba, it's extremely
difficult, expensive, and frustrating to find

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.460
a supplier.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:49.640
Alibaba cut out the middleman.

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:54.199
They make it extremely easy to find, communicate,
and negotiate with suppliers directly through

00:07:54.199 --> 00:07:55.199
their website.”

00:07:55.199 --> 00:07:57.080
Jae Jun, businessman and investor.)

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:01.110
Then in China… in addition to the local
wholesale market, which in this case is known

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:07.110
as 1688.com, Alibaba has two of the largest
retail electronic commerce markets in the

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:10.379
country: Taobao and Tmall.

00:08:10.379 --> 00:08:15.900
See, Taobao is pretty much a combination between
Amazon and eBay.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:20.460
Here, practically anyone can sell their products...
it’s a market with thousands and thousands

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:24.610
of suppliers and almost 600 million active
consumers.

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:30.060
Tmall, on the other hand, is a large online
shopping center oriented towards big brands.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:32.860
Here the brands pay a fee to have their own
store.

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.760
Basically like any shopping mall.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:37.290
Then, one of the lesser-known crown jewels...

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:42.390
Alibaba owns more than 80% of Lazada, the
most important e-commerce company in South

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:43.390
Asia.

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:45.500
A company that operates in countries like
Indonesia, Vietnam, Malaysia, Singapore and

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.500
Thailand.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.540
And watch out, because we aren’t talking
about something small scale.

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:55.080
Only in the next 2 to 3 years... these countries
will see their middle class multiply by 2...

00:08:55.080 --> 00:09:00.630
to surpass 400 million people... 400 million
people that Alibaba wants to turn into their

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:01.630
customers.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:06.280
And finally, we have what is probably the
best-known platform for most of us: Ali Express,

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:08.820
an international consumer-oriented platform.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:18.060
Well, these, folks, are Alibaba’s main “markets”,
but the company's activities don’t end here.

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:22.220
Alibaba is also one of the 5 most important
Cloud Computing companies in the world and,

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:24.620
of course, it’s China’s undisputed leader.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:31.280
And this division’s growth rate has surpassed
100% annually in recent years.

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:38.270
Companies such as KPMG, Nestle, Philips and
SAP already use Alicloud’s services.

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:42.920
It also owns Youku, a streaming platform similar
to Youtube, owned by Ele.me, China's largest

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:46.720
home delivery company, which, among many other
companies, also holds a significant share

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:50.040
of Weibo, something like the Chinese Facebook.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.670
But... just a second.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:53.410
Have you ever heard of Alipay?

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:57.030
For those who don’t know what it is, Alipay
is very similar to Paypal... it has more than

00:09:57.030 --> 00:10:02.960
870 million active users and is the leader
in the Chinese mobile payment market.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:07.720
Because see, in China… credit cards aren’t
common at all…

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:12.150
The Chinese have jumped directly to mobile
payments.... so when they go to the supermarket,

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:16.560
instead of paying with Visa or Mastercard,
they use Alipay or Wechat's payment services,

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:19.610
the two main payment services in the Chinese
market.

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:20.610
Well...

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:26.490
Alibaba owns 33% of Ant Financial, the company
that owns Alipay and also Paytm, the leading

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:29.680
mobile payment application in India... another
strongly growing market.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:31.810
To give you an idea of what this means…

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:37.180
Ant Financial’s estimated value surpasses
150 billion dollars.

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:42.110
But... just a moment, because if this entire
online bet wasn’t enough…

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:46.470
Alibaba is also investing billions in supermarkets
and other physical stores... where it has

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:51.640
its own brand, Hema, and is also the largest
shareholder in the Sun Art Retail Group, the

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:55.880
largest supermarket and hypermarket operator
in all of China.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:11:01.420
So, as you can see, the Alibaba empire extends
its tentacles to a lot of sectors.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:06.870
To sum things up, Alibaba has services equivalent
to those of Amazon, eBay, Just Eat, Visa,

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:10.560
YouTube, Facebook and even Carrefour... all
in the same company...

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:11.730
Not bad, right?

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:16.270
Well, that’s precisely why this company
is worth more than 400 billion dollars in

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:17.270
the stock market.

00:11:17.270 --> 00:11:18.270
But...

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:26.370
I don’t think we can end this story without
talking about the future…

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:32.590
(RISKS AND OPPORTUNITIES)

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:36.270
However we look at it, Alibaba's plans are
very ambitious.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:44.510
By 2020, sales made through Alibaba's different
platforms will exceed one trillion dollars.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:53.830
And in just 18 years the company aims to surpass
2 billion customers.

00:11:53.830 --> 00:12:01.080
Yes... that’s the goal.

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:02.140
Will it achieve it?

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:05.620
Obviously we can’t know… but the truth
is that it has many cards on the table.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:10.480
See… despite the company’s huge growth
since its foundation in 1999, it still has

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:11.550
great potential.

00:12:11.550 --> 00:12:15.460
Not only because e-commerce is growing a lot
around the world... but also because everything

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:22.940
indicates that growth will be explosive for
many years, particularly in this region.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:25.950
Let's take a look at, for example, China,
Alibaba’s main market.

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:30.680
Here the Internet has only expanded by 55%,
so there’s still a lot of work to do.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:34.380
We’re talking about hundreds of millions
of people who will sooner or later connect

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:38.050
to the internet and start making their first
online purchases.

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:43.910
And not only that, given that Chinese purchasing
power is growing stronger, year after year,

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:47.170
the same is happening with the average amounts
of purchases...

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:53.120
See, since 2015, the average Alibaba customer’s
spending has grown by 50% in China...

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.970
So if we combine more spending and more clients...

00:12:55.970 --> 00:13:01.230
You can see how enormous the potential is
here.

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:05.590
And then, in addition, there are the countries
which belong to the Association of Southeast

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:07.870
Asian Nations and also India, etc..

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:10.650
We’re talking about an area of the world
that isn’t only going to experience as a

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:15.560
huge economic entity but also, that is estimated
to grow by more than 700 million people in

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:16.850
the next three decades.

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:20.670
All of this, in addition to the international
market, of course.

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:23.270
Now... just a second, because everything isn’t
so… rosy.

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:26.540
Like many Internet companies, who focus all
their attention on growing and growing...

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:37.930
the company isn’t making much money...

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:42.050
In this case we’re talking about a 400 billion
dollar company that has barely managed to

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:45.600
make a net profit of 8.4 billion dollars in
the last 12 months.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:50.630
Yes, that may sound like a lot of money, but
the market value is 50 times the net profit...

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:51.630
and that's... a lot.

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:54.730
And of course... one might think, okay, okay...
but so what?

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.240
It’ll make money in the future...

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:58.710
Well, maybe... or maybe not.

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:03.550
Because if a market grows so much, it usually
entails a very strong incentive for new competitors,

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:08.260
new rivals… something that is already happening
in a certain way.

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:13.900
Look, competitors like JD.com and especially
Pinduoduo, are investing a lot of money to

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:18.760
compete with Alibaba... and even though they
are very successful, they may never beat Alibaba

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:22.770
– or maybe they will – the truth is that,
no matter what, it adds more pressure to the

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:28.920
market, which may reduce the margins in which
these companies operate in the future.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:32.100
And then, of course, there’s the Chinese
government... which, as you know, isn’t

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.480
precisely the best guarantor in the world.

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:38.440
As you know, the Chinese government does and
undoes as it pleases... and that can even

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:41.420
determine who survives in a market and who
doesn’t.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:46.130
That means that a botched delivery to a Communist
Party leader could become Alibaba’s worst

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:47.130
nightmare...

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:56.240
In any case, it’s clear that Alibaba is
the best example of the changes that our world

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:57.240
is experiencing.

00:14:57.240 --> 00:15:01.810
Of how Asia is gaining power… and of how
it’s beginning to acquire its own large

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:03.180
multinationals...

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:05.440
And we better get used to it.

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:08.870
So I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did, and don’t forget to

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:10.480
subscribe for brand new videos.

